---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
export function getStaticPaths() {
  return [
    { params: { slug: "session-security" }, props: { category: "ENGINEERING", title: "A better way to think about session security", date: "October 21, 2026", intro: "A good session gives the user a smooth return and the product a reliable way to end access. Those goals should be designed together." } },
    { params: { slug: "invisible-identity" }, props: { category: "PRODUCT", title: "Identity should feel invisible", date: "October 8, 2026", intro: "Authentication is the first promise your product makes: your account is yours, and we will protect it." } },
    { params: { slug: "organization-authorization" }, props: { category: "ENGINEERING", title: "Multi-tenant authorization starts with ownership", date: "September 24, 2026", intro: "A tenant boundary is only as strong as the rules attached to it. Model ownership and membership explicitly." } },
  ];
}
const { title, category, date, intro } = Astro.props;
---
<Base title={`${title} — Arbeiter Journal`}><article class="article"><a href="/" class="back">← &nbsp;All stories</a><div class="art"><div class="ring"></div></div><div class="meta"><span>{category}</span><span>{date} · 5 MIN READ</span></div><h1>{title}</h1><p class="intro">{intro}</p><div class="body"><p>Trust is built in the details. Authentication systems need to keep the user experience simple while preserving the properties that matter: credentials stay protected, sessions can be revoked, and sensitive actions require clear intent.</p><h2>Start with the boundary</h2><p>Keep identity operations behind one well-defined API. Give the client a small, understandable surface and let the server own the sensitive decisions. Every request should carry enough context for the server to apply authorization consistently.</p><p>From there, build flows that communicate status to users. A session should be visible, expiration should be predictable, and account changes should have a straightforward path to recovery.</p><h2>Make the secure choice the easy choice</h2><p>Good defaults give teams a solid base: secure cookies, short-lived action tokens, thoughtful rate limits, and audit events that are useful without collecting secrets. Keep the product experience focused, then let developers extend it where they need to.</p><a class="cta" href="http://localhost:4322">Explore the API documentation ↗</a></div></article></Base>
<style>.article{max-width:700px;margin:42px auto 90px;padding:0 24px}.back{font-size:11px;text-decoration:none;color:#7668d6}.art{height:260px;background:#f0efff;border-radius:11px;margin:24px 0;display:grid;place-items:center;overflow:hidden}.ring{width:120px;height:120px;border:1px solid #7567e0;border-radius:50%;position:relative}.ring:before,.ring:after{content:"";position:absolute;inset:-30px 15px;border:1px solid #b3acf3;border-radius:50%;transform:rotate(55deg)}.ring:after{transform:rotate(-55deg);inset:15px -30px}.meta{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:9px;letter-spacing:.9px;color:#999faf}.meta span:first-child{color:#5e4bd6;font-weight:700}h1{font:800 37px/1.15 Manrope;letter-spacing:-1.2px;margin:18px 0}.intro{font:500 16px/1.7 Manrope;color:#727d8e;border-left:2px solid #7564e4;padding-left:17px}.body{color:#586477;font-size:13px;line-height:1.9;margin-top:30px}.body h2{font:700 20px Manrope;color:#1d2737;margin-top:30px}.cta{display:inline-block;background:#5b49db;color:white;border-radius:7px;padding:12px 16px;text-decoration:none;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;margin-top:10px}@media(max-width:600px){.article{margin-top:25px}.art{height:200px}h1{font-size:30px}}</style>
